## What Already Exists vs. What Needs to Be Built

### Already exists in the platform (just needs MCP wrapping)
Everything in `claims_core_mcp`, `vendor_mcp`, `expert_dispatch_mcp`, `stp_mcp`, `decision_mcp`, `cost_estimation_mcp`, `communication_mcp`, and `fraud_mcp` — the underlying REST API endpoints and DB tables are fully built. These tools are wrappers around existing `/api/*` endpoints.

### Needs to be built from scratch
`fnol_mcp` — the FNOL AI inference tables exist, but there's no LLM-backed logic yet to fill them.
`document_analysis_mcp` — GCS file storage exists, but document parsing, image analysis, and LLM-based cross-referencing logic needs to be implemented (following the `attachment_summary_mcp` pattern in the parent Jarvis project).

